{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And I will hide My face from them.</b> This is a way of affection — like a person whose son sinned against him, and he says to his teacher to strike him, but he himself cannot bear to see his son's suffering, for his compassion is upon him, so he hides his face so as not to see the beating of his son." "<b>Many evils and troubles.</b> Evils that became troubles to one another — for example, a wasp and a scorpion: cold water helps for a wasp sting, and hot water for a scorpion sting, and the opposite is dangerous. One who was stung by both a wasp and a scorpion does not know what to do, for what helps this one harms that one. And so are the troubles of Israel in exile: when the idolaters oppress him, he fears to cry out against him lest he make him hate him, and if he does not cry out against him, he will grow accustomed to oppressing him." "<b>Because Elohim is not within me.</b> That I caused Him to remove His Shekhinah from me — ״באו עלי״ etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:38.995513867Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}